> > I actually know exactly what's causing this and it can be solved by upgrading to the latest DBI version on CRAN (or latest development version will do too). Basically, DBI > 0.6 breaks back compatibility because they change a method signature (the error above). As soon as that was released on CRAN, I also updated pool to be compatible with the current DBI.
> >
> > So, it seems that that user has an old version of DBI and the current version of pool.
> >
> > That error can reproed with these commands:
> >
> > > # With DBI < 0.6, trying to install pool results in an error
> > > devtools::install_github("cran/DBI@882c3921ee58d1fa97298697bf2a50161a8e401a")
> > > devtools::install_github("rstudio/pool")
> >
> > By upgrading DBI, the problem goes away:
> >
> > > # With current DBI, all is good
