We don't have built in analytics within of shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io>. However, we do support setting up Google Analytics <https://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/google-analytics.html> to track usage of your application. That probably wont help tracking down this specific user, but it can be insightful.

-Andy

On Wed, May 31, 2017 at 1:53 AM, Alejandro Ruete <aler...@gmail.com> wrote:

> Hello,
> I have a couple of apps in shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io> and I have noticed that there is a repetitive and constant pattern of usage on two of my apps.
>
>  <https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-2AiqrzhLCuM/WS6Cg6qNjKI/AAAAAAAAL4U/8wSulUOPnUgd8q8flCLssjt9paUzdSPvgCLcB/s1600/Untitled.png>
>
>
> As you can see in this screen capture, it seem that every week day the apps are used during the max sleep time (15 mins x 2 = 0.5 hs), once, twice or even three times a day. My suspicion is that somebody has them open in a browser that refresh them every time the computer awakes, and then the server close the connection. I will of course reduce the idle time limit, but I wonder if there is any way I can track the user, or precent this kind of uses having a Free account.
>
> Thanks

